==Overview==
<tabber> 
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Chop was the best fruit to use when fighting with another sword user.
* Chop's passive ability granted immunity to all attacks from [[Swords|swords]], including attacks from all players and [[NPC's]] with [[Aura]] as long as the user was ~105% - 106% of the [[NPC's]] level, similar to [[Elemental]] effects.
* Fairly cheap.
* Decent damage.

|'''[Z] Tackle'''
* Decent damage and relatively short cooldown.

|'''[X] Dance'''
* Good stun.

|'''[C] Party'''
* Decent stun.

|'''[F] Helicopter'''
* A low-mastery flight move.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* All of Chop's moves had a very limited range and were relatively easy to avoid.
* Weak in air.
* Some sword moves can still stun the user. An example of this is [[Rengoku]]'s '''[Z] Demon Slayer''' move.
* [[Ice]], [[Light]] and the [[Canvander]] sword of Besto Friendo from [[Love]]'s melee attacks bypassed Chop's passive ability as they count as [[Blox Fruits|fruit]] attacks.
* [[Bosses]] and [[Raid Bosses]] were not affected by the passive ability.

|'''[Z] Tackle'''
* Extremely bad range.

|'''[X] Dance'''
* The user could not cancel the move once it was used, which made it very easy to counter back if not hit the enemy.
* Extremely slow.

|'''[C] Party'''
* Bad range.

|'''[F] Helicopter'''
* Low speed.
* Not recommended to use for transportation.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia== 
* Although Chop's passive function was to avoid damage from sword slashes, Chop could also avoid swords that can create fire, freeze, cause electric shock, and even magic damage.
* Chop was mostly known because of its sword immunity.
* It was recommended to become a sword main instead of a fruit user when using Chop.
* Most attacks looked weird with R15 and layered clothing since the user's body stretched and did not disconnect.
* Chop was a very good replacement for [[elemental]] fruits to use at a low level since most enemies use swords in the [[First Sea]], although it got bad quickly, getting outclassed in every way by higher rarity fruits because of its lack of abilities, and the fact that later NPCs ([[Second Sea]] and [[Third Sea]]) more commonly use [[Fighting Styles]].
* Chop's X move was similar to [[Shark Saw]]'s [X] move.
* [[Bobby]], a Lv. 55 [[Boss]], used Chop before [[Updates/26|Update 26]].
* Chop and [[Rocket]] were the only fruits in which the [F] move has the highest mastery requirements out of all the other move.
* Chop is one of the only fruits whose reworks completely removed it from the game as [[Chef]] (Reworked [[Bobby]]) no longer uses it.
* This fruit has the same fruit design even if it was reworked, similar to [https://blox-fruits.fandom.com/wiki/Rumble Rumble] (Now [[Lightning]]).

